    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0212" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/404.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Reid.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d107-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon states that owing to the death of the Empress Dowager and the Emperor
                    of China<anchor n="2" xml:id="d107-f2"/> the Wai-wu Pu has requested that the
                    sitting of the opium commission be postponed to the 1st of February next. Says
                    that while the United States regrets the necessity of interfering with the
                    program laid down it sympathizes with the Chinese Government in its bereavement
                    and considers such postponement would be desirable if acceptable to
                    participating powers. Mr. Reid is instructed to communicate this suggestion to
                    the foreign office and deport telegraphically the attitude of the British
                    Government.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d107-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d107-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to France, Germany, Russia, Japan, Persia, The Netherlands, Portugal,
                    and Siam.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d107-f2" n="2" xml:id="d107-f2-content">
